Subject: chunk: default temporary directory on VMS is SYS$SCRATCH

Request bodies over the in-memory limit (uploads, large POSTs to
FastCGI) go to temporary files in server.upload-dirs, which defaults to
$TMPDIR, else /var/tmp.  OpenVMS has no /var/tmp, so -tt warned
"server.upload-dirs /var/tmp: no such file or directory" and uploads
would fail unless upload-dirs was set.  getenv("TMPDIR") on VMS also
finds a logical name, so DEFINE TMPDIR still works; without it use
SYS$SCRATCH, every process's scratch directory.

--- a/src/chunk.c
+++ b/src/chunk.c
@@ -759,6 +759,9 @@
     #ifdef _WIN32
     if (NULL == env_tmpdir) env_tmpdir = getenv("TEMP");
     #endif
+  #ifdef __VMS
+    if (NULL == env_tmpdir) env_tmpdir = "/sys$scratch";
+  #endif
     if (NULL == env_tmpdir) env_tmpdir = "/var/tmp";
 }
 
